WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.960
We've finally made it.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.640
After 48 episodes,
two robberies

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.840
and one man disguising
himself as a couch,

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.080
yes that happened,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.240
Money Heist reached
its thrilling conclusion.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.560
This is not just
the end of season five,̧

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.640
but of all Money Heist,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.480
and what a series
to go out on.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.480
The Professor got to boogie,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.600
Berlin had the world's first
one-man bar fight,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.240
and we enjoyed the funkiest
rendition of Bella Ciao yet.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.120
Even with the cops
at the door,

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.760
there's no stopping
the grooviest robbers on TV.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.040
Money Heist's final run

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.200
also delivered answers
we've been waiting for:

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.240
how to get the gold
out of the bank,

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.200
how to get the robbers
out of the bank

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.640
and just what was
the relevance

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.840
of all those
Berlin flashbacks.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.760
With the series wrapped up

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.320
and our thieves
scattered to the wind,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.640
it's time to take a look
at the final episodes

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.600
and break down
the masterstrokes

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.520
of The Professor's
greatest plan yet.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.480
As if it needs to be said,
beware spoilers!

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.440
Let's start with
the first part of the plan.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.800
How do you get 90 tonnes
of gold out of a bank?

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.840
Turns out it takes
a smelter,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.240
an industrial oil pump,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.160
some complicated maths

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.480
and one very virile
oil rig worker.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.400
Seven kids
with seven different women.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.840
From the moment
the gang crack

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.080
the flooded vault
in part three,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.800
and started melting the gold
into tiny pellets,

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.320
it was obvious
they weren't going

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.160
to transport the gold
via traditional means.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.440
They were very open
about the fact.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.880
Lisbon explained it
to the court

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.560
before being rescued
using the Paris plan.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.600
The plan is to steal
90 tonnes of gold

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.880
from the national reserve.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.160
We're melting it.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.840
And the Professor spilled
the tiny golden beans

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.080
to Sierra,

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.680
but she chose
not to believe him.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.080
It'll come out
mushed up with the water.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.080
You think I'm stupid, right?

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.560
The answer came
in episode six of part five,

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.520
where Berlin visited an
oil rig in the Barent's Sea

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.880
a whole five years before
the Bank of Spain heist.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.760
Here, we learn two things.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.600
One, that Berlin makes

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.440
for a hugely fun passenger
on long trips.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.000
And two, that the pumps
used by the rig have

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.720
the power to shift liquids
at high pressure.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.320
This thing sucks stuff
from the seabed

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.640
as if it were baby food.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.640
By mixing pellets
with vault water,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.400
the robbers fill the drain
pipes under the bank

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.640
with gold.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.360
This process uses
a small pump

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.840
which doesn't have the force
needed to push that gold

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.320
through the 11 miles of pipe

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.800
from the bank
to the storm water tank,

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.440
which is where Benjamin and
the gang are waiting for it.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.880
Enter the industrial pump,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.680
with the raw power to flush
the remaining vault water

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.600
and the pipe gold all the
way to the storm water tank

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:10.960
Too little pressure

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.320
and the gold
won't get there.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.520
Too much
and the pipes will explode.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.320
The tricky part is manually
controlling pressure

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.120
and calculating the values.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.560
Palermo cites
Darcy Weisbach

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.320
which is an equation
in fluid dynamics

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.560
used to find
the impact of friction

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.720
on liquids
moving through a pipe.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:29.840
For once,

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.120
The Professor has met
his galaxy-brained match.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.520
Am I crazy or am I
the only one who sees this?

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.400
The final twist in the plan?

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.680
Instead of pumping
the gold downhill,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.600
where the police
are more likely to look,

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.400
Palermo chooses
to pump it upstream.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.000
We'll get the gold up the
river like fucking salmons,

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.880
to the storm water tank.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.080
So when the police turn up

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.760
at the wrong
storm water tank,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.560
there's not
a single gold ball in sight.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.120
Of course,
maths only gets you so far.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.760
To Palermo,
the plan is a love letter

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.080
to his time with Berlin

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.000
and it's his faith in that
plan and that relationship

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.040
that pushes
the gang and the gold

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.800
to where they need to be.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.800
Speaking of Berlin,
the drainpipe plan feels

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.240
like an echo
of his earlier robbery

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.920
at Frederiksborg castle…

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.880
where he stole Viking
treasure with his son,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.400
then used the river outside

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.280
to safely transport their
swag to another location.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.520
And speaking of Raphael,
now's a good time to address

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.280
a tiny problem
in The Professor's plan.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.880
No sooner have they
extracted the gold by pipe

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.360
and smelted it
back into ingots,

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.440
the team is robbed
by another gang of thieves

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.760
posing as policemen.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.520
Yes, the irony
of robbers being robbed

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.200
isn't lost on us.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.880
Our gold's been stolen.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.520
The culprit?

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.560
Berlin's son Raphael
and former wife, Tatiana.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.520
-We did it!
-We did it!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.640
To pick this twist apart,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.400
let's rewind
back a few years.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:02.840
In part three,

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.360
we're introduced to Berlin's
new bride, Tatiana,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.960
during one of the show's
many flashbacks.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:09.720
On the plus side,

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.320
it means we get another
Berlin musical number.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.560
But The Professor is alarmed
that Berlin has shared

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.480
his plans
for the Bank of Spain heist

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:24.720
with an outsider.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.800
By the way, she loves
the Bank of Spain heist.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.360
She knows.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.320
Staying in the past,

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.160
but jumping
forwards a few months,

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:40.520
Berlin introduces Tatiana
to his son, Raphael.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.040
He needs them both
to rob the Danish castle.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.640
But while the Copenhagen job
goes without a hitch,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.800
it ignites a spark between
Raphael and Tatiana,

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.600
and nervous looks
in the boat

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.920
blossom
into a full-on affair.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.040
We'd feel bad for Berlin

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.000
but it's only what he taught
his son to do.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.240
If you really want
something in life...

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.720
you have to steal it
from whoever has it.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.200
This results

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.760
in the most expensive
bar bill in history

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.120
for a heartbroken Berlin.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.120
But in a way,

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.120
it also triggers the entire
Money Heist story.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.080
Berlin's broken heart

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.320
and stint in jail
for smashing the bar

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.160
is what opens him up
to working

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.320
with his brother,
The Professor,

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.440
on the original
Royal Mint heist.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.200
Before I die,

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:27.440
you and I are going to rob
the Royal Mint of Spain.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.240
Yes,
Money Heist is basically

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.040
just a really messy breakup.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.560
Eating a massive tub
of Haagen-Dazs

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.640
would have been much easier.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.560
Back in the present,
we have fun

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.320
seeing The Professor lose
his cool for a minute.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.440
She's a pianist.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.560
And a thief!

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.680
But it's also neat seeing
the family resemblance

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.800
between his work
and Raphael's.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.000
The idea of Raphael
observing the crime scene

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.520
from a bank of monitors

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.760
is a classic Professor move.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.840
as is
the attention to detail

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.240
when he and Tatiana hide
the gold under the house.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.520
The total commitment
to the disguise is the same

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.320
as The Professor dressing
as a homeless man

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.840
back in season one,

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.600
to, yes, stapling
himself and Sierra

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.960
inside the couch.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.960
Of course, Sierra
does get the gold back.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:22.880
After The Professor realises

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.680
Raphael and Tatiana
must be hiding the loot,

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.160
Sierra tracks it by looking
for recently purchased land

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.000
and confronts
the pair of lovebirds.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.800
And reclaiming the ingots
is crucial to the plan.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.400
It's the answer
to the other huge question

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.800
hanging over the heist:

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.600
how to get the robbers
out of the bank.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.280
Because while you may be
able to squeeze gold pellets

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.400
through 11 miles of pipe,

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.680
Helsinki is
more of a challenge.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.360
Without the gold,
we're done for.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.720
Then we're done for.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.400
The short answer is

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.280
they plan to hold the gold
hostage outside the bank

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.920
to secure the release of
the robbers inside the bank.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.400
That might sound
like backwards thinking,

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.800
but you have to remember
the whole point

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.320
of robbing the Spanish
Reserve in the first place

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:07.400
was to use it as a
bargaining chip to free Rio.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.680
The gold was never
the real target.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.240
For his plan to work,

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.040
The Professor needs
to apply financial pressure

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.360
to the Spanish government.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.480
It's not enough
to take the gold.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:18.680
As Tamayo explains,

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.720
the government have
safety nets in place.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.880
Bad news.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.280
I've got the support
of the European Central Bank

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.360
to inject cash or buy debt.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.440
To amplify
the financial crisis,

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.400
the robbers broadcast

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.840
their successful
gold heist online.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.440
In fact, watch back
through the series,

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.280
and you'll often see
characters filming

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.720
on their mobile phones.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.400
No, it wasn't just
inappropriate TikToks,

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:42.960
they were documenting
their heist.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.960
To further destabilise
the financial market,

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.160
The Professor plants
fake clues

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.080
to draw the police and army
to search

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:50.680
for the gold in the ocean.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.080
Filling the storm water tank

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.840
with charred remains
of fake documents

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.960
reminds us of The Professor
planting fake leads

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.240
in his hideout

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.080
during the Royal Mint heist.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.440
He loves a wild goose chase.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.520
The plan is named
after Tom Thumb,

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.880
or as he's known in Spain,

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.200
Pulgarcito.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.560
The original
Tom Thumb story's

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:11.080
where a tiny,
thumb-sized man

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.720
goes on wild adventures,

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.440
where he was passed
from bird to fish.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.040
which could relate

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.320
to the long journey
Marseille leads Angel on

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.920
in pursuit of the gold.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.200
But the Tom Thumb story's

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.720
also seen as a tale
about how a tiny hero

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.760
can take on
massive challenges.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.240
Which does link nicely

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:29.920
to a handful of robbers
bringing down

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.640
a financial market.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:33.840
With the stock market
plummeting,

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.640
The Professor can negotiate
with Tamayo

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.520
and offers to return it

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.320
in exchange
for their freedom.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.360
This is why
the whole plan hinges

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.760
on retrieving the gold
from Raphael and Tatiana.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:46.760
No bargaining chip,
no escape.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.080
Which leads us
to the final twist.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.360
The gold is returned,

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.360
despite currently being
buried under a house

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.600
and trapped in a standoff
between Sierra and Tatiana.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.280
Yeah, it confused us too.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.080
But this is the brilliance
of The Professor's plan.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.800
He returns brass
coated in gold,

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:05.680
an idea he had

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.400
after noticing how his
food tins resembled ingots.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:10.960
It's also an idea

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.760
with a proven
Money Heist track record.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:16.040
Berlin's Copenhagen job
swapped Viking treasure

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.320
for brass fakes.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.560
The twist hinges
on the concept

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.280
that the gold in the reserve
is more of an idea

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:22.720
than a valuable thing.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:24.760
Countries don't spend it,

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.600
it just sits there,
underpinning the economy.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.120
Throughout the series,
people are remarking

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.280
how no one can truly own
the gold.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.480
After all, it just fell from
space millions of years ago.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.560
And as Palermo notes

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:38.560
of historic gold…

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.000
This gold
was already stolen once.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.800
It can't be stolen twice.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.760
Finally, there's Lisbon

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.760
dropping a neat literary
reference to Tamayo.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:48.400
Lazarillo de Tormes

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.440
wasn't written
by the English.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:51.920
Was it?

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.040
Lazarillo de Tormes
is a novella

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.680
from the Spanish Golden Age

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.160
and follows
a young boy mastering

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.600
the art of thievery.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.440
It was so influential,
it invented an entire genre,

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.880
the picaresque novel,

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.600
taken from the word picaro

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:06.800
meaning "rogue".

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:08.480
She's almost making the case

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.880
that ingenious deception
and improvisation,

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.120
the skills
that define The Professor,

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.760
are a key part of the
Spanish national character.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:16.800
And so it is

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.720
they convince Tamayo
to work with them.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.640
While the robbers fake
their deaths

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:21.960
to let him walk
away from the siege

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:22.920
with a bit of pride,

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.320
he also has to accept
the fake gold

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.040
in the name
of stabilising the markets.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:30.640
And because the robbers
reclaimed the real gold

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.160
from Raphael and Tatiana,

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.960
they can use it
as a safety net.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:37.240
They just need to expose its
existence outside the bank

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:38.800
to ruin the economy again.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:41.760
And it's this that finally
secures their future.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.880
It's one hell of a plan.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.120
And so we reach the end
of the Bank of Spain heist.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.440
It was not without
a few tears along the way,

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.720
rest in peace
Nairobi and Tokyo,

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.080
but it's also not the
bloodbath some expected.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:58.800
There was
a popular fan theory

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.200
that more characters
would die.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.320
Some people felt

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.080
the two teams of footballers
in part four

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.320
represented
who would live or die.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.880
And others felt Nairobi's
heavenly flashback

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.240
pointed towards The
Professor's eventual death.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.160
But it was not to be.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.600
The biggest question
we still have

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.600
is why they never blocked up
those air vents.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:20.040
Between Gandia, Stockholm
and Arantxe Arteche,

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.520
there was always someone
in the walls

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.160
during parts four and five.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:26.960
Air vents, you are
the real MVP of Money Heist.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.560
And that brings us to the
end of our Ending Explained.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.520
Why not watch
our earlier theories videos

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.320
to see how they stacked up?

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.400
Well, after you've done

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:37.640
an entire Money Heist
series re-watch, of course.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.480
For more videos like this,

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:41.360
subscribe
to Netflix: Still Watching

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:43.040
and we'll see you soon.

